   "id": 522480,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Consider a cross to investigate the pea pod texture trait, involving constricted or inflated pods. Mendel found that the traits behave according to a dominant/recessive pattern in which inflated pods were dominant. If you performed this cross and obtained 650 inflated-pod plants in the <span data-math=\"F_2\">F_2</span> generation bred from true-breeding stock, approximately how many constricted-pod plants would you expect to have?",
